    "script": "sse-bridge-proto-6c912d",
    "durableObjectNamespace": "fb0d60f014ee4c62ab1b0314636a91bb",
    "source": "Throwaway Worker + minimal SQLite Durable Object (not CamelAgent; nothing of the pilot was touched). The object accepts sockets with ctx.acceptWebSocket and a ping/pong auto-response, and holds SSE responses with a 30 s heartbeat comment. Four objects, one client each, from one Node client: websocket-direct (client WebSocket forwarded by the Worker to the object, client ping every 30 s), sse-direct (the object holds the SSE response), sse-bridge (the Worker opens a WebSocket to the object with stub.fetch + Upgrade, accept()s it and writes frames as SSE; heartbeat comment from the Worker every 30 s), sse-bridge-wsping (the same, and the Worker also sends \"ping\" upstream every 30 s, answered by the auto-response). After the idle period one event was sent to each object; the event carries the object instance id, which changes only when the object was evicted."
  },
